     1,
     "<br>\r\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><font face=\"Default Sans Serif,Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\r\n<div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"BORDER-LEFT:#000000 2px solid;PADDING-LEFT:5px;PADDING-RIGHT:0px;MARGIN-LEFT:5px;MARGIN-RIGHT:0px\">To: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a><br>From: Andy Royle/BRD/USGS/DOI<br>\r\nDate: 09/27/2012 06:49AM<br>Subject: Re: [unmarked] gmultimix question - using gmultmix to model spatial subsampling<br><br><font face=\"Default Sans Serif,Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\r\n<div><br></div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>hi Rob, </div>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>I agree with you the &quot;availability&quot; or psi parameter is the probability that an individual in the grid population is available at the point during sampling.  This transposing that you do to fit the model implies a sensible model of spatial sub-sampling which I hadn&#39;t thought of before. [note I added some words to your Subject so people might find this post for &quot;subsampling&quot;]</div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>To answer your 2nd question -- are all of the points and their count radii within the grid cell? If so then I think the E[N] applies to the grid cell.  If the point circles are slopping over the edge of the grid cell then this is a tougher question to answer. I would say in that case E[N] probably applies to the area of the grid buffered by 60m.  </div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n<div>The parameter psi accounts for imperfect spatial coverage of the sample frame.</div>\r\n<div>regards</div>\r\n<div>andy</div>\r\n<div><br> </div><font color=\"#990099\">-----<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a> wrote: -----<br><br></font>\r\n<blockquote style=\"BORDER-LEFT:#000000 2px solid;PADDING-LEFT:5px;PADDING-RIGHT:0px;MARGIN-LEFT:5px;MARGIN-RIGHT:0px\">To: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a><br>From: Rob Sparks &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">robs...@hotmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\nSent by: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a><br>Date: 09/25/2012 02:35PM<br>Subject: [unmarked] gmultimix question<br><br>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I have a question on the gmultmix function and particularly if I could trade time for space in the following way.  We have a 1km grid and within each grid we have 16 points and at each point we have minute intervals.  I was thinking of using the 1km grid as the sites, points as the primary periods and the minute intervals as the secondary periods.  Below is a subset of my data, column one is site identifier,column A1 is point 1 minute interval 1, A2 is point 1 minute interval 2, A3 is point 1 minute interval 3 and so on for each of the 16 points.  </p>\r\n\r\n<table style=\"BORDER-COLLAPSE:collapse;MARGIN-LEFT:4.65pt\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"MIN-HEIGHT:15pt\">\r\n<td style=\"PADDING-BOTTOM:0in;MIN-HEIGHT:15pt;PADDING-LEFT:5.4pt;PADDING-RIGHT:5.4pt;PADDING-TOP:0in\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN-BOTTOM:0pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\">           <span>Transect<u></u><u></u><u></u></span></p></td>\r\n<td style=\"PADDING-BOTTOM:0in;MIN-HEIGHT:15pt;PADDING-LEFT:5.4pt;PADDING-RIGHT:5.4pt;PADDING-TOP:0in\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN-BOTTOM:0pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>A1<u></u><u></u></span></p></td>\r\n<td style=\"PADDING-BOTTOM:0in;MIN-HEIGHT:15pt;PADDING-LEFT:5.4pt;PADDING-RIGHT:5.4pt;PADDING-TOP:0in\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN-BOTTOM:0pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>A2<u></u><u></u></span></p></td>\r\n<td style=\"PADDING-BOTTOM:0in;MIN-HEIGHT:15pt;PADDING-LEFT:5.4pt;PADDING-RIGHT:5.4pt;PADDING-TOP:0in\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p style=\"LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN-BOTTOM:0pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>A3<u></u><u></u></span></p></td>\r\n<td style=\"PADDING-BOTTOM:0in;MIN-HEIGHT:15pt;PADDING-LEFT:5.4