style=\"PADDING-BOTTOM:0in;MIN-HEIGHT:15pt;PADDING-LEFT:5.4pt;PADDING-RIGHT:5.4pt;PADDING-TOP:0in\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:right;LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN-BOTTOM:0pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"right\"><span>0<u></u><u></u></span></p></td>\r\n<td style=\"PADDING-BOTTOM:0in;MIN-HEIGHT:15pt;PADDING-LEFT:5.4pt;PADDING-RIGHT:5.4pt;PADDING-TOP:0in\" valign=\"bottom\" nowrap>\r\n<p style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:right;LINE-HEIGHT:normal;MARGIN-BOTTOM:0pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"right\"><span>0<u></u><u></u></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">One question is if I set up my dataset this way is the availability parameter being estimated across sites or across primary periods (points)?  I think it is among primary periods (points) but wanted to double check.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Another question is since we collected distance data as well I truncated the detections at each point to be within a 120 meter radius.  So I think the abundance estimate is at this scale and not at the 1km grid scale is that correct? So if I wanted density at the 1km grid could I use an offset?  Or how can I go about getting this?</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks for any insight the group may have.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Rob</p></blockquote><br></div></font></blockquote><br></div></font></div><br>\r\n"
